From 2f401857e77c2b0df6c772c3638142b94e68c7bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 21:41:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(camera): decode instructions and resolve server fades
 and FOV transitions

Protocol 2193 carries independent optional camera fields, including named
spline references, little-endian signed actor IDs and string-encoded FOV
and keyframe easing. Decode every instruction field before applying the
fade, retain the decoded instruction for integrations, and bound spline
allocations. Presets, movement, splines and shake remain separate implementation gaps.

Resolve overlapping fades in core and send versioned timeline snapshots
to subscribed clients after joining and channel registration. Late
subscribers receive elapsed state instead of restarting the effect. Keep
ordinary Java clients connected when no native rendering client subscribes.

The matching Bedrock 1.26.51.1 server emitted seven captured instructions.
Its executable's fade insertion and updater confirm minimum duration,
current-opacity continuity, retained color and later fade-out completion.
Targeted tests compare native schedules and samples without distributing
native binaries, assets or captures.

Resolve FOV clamping, easing, repeated commands and clear lifecycle with a
shared core transition model. Transport elapsed snapshots and live commands
to subscribed rendering clients. Retain the local projection symbolically
when core lacks client context. Live commands capture the rendered client
projection; clear captures its normal projection. Native 1.26.51.1 updater
and easing probes supply private comparison fixtures for targeted tests.
